  "title": "Debug: BCD Adder with Faulty Correction Logic",
  "description": "The pre-wired circuit is meant to be a single-digit BCD adder built with two 7483 ICs. It works correctly for sums up to 9, but for sums of 10 or more it produces an invalid binary result instead of a BCD result. Three faults have been introduced: (1) the correction detector uses an AND gate where an OR gate is required, (2) the correction word wired to the second 7483 is 0011 instead of 0110, and (3) the Carry-In of the second 7483 is left floating instead of being grounded. Inspect the circuit, find the faults and fix them so that the outputs match the BCD truth table.",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "debug",
  "tags": [
    "Debugging",
    "BCD Adder",
    "7483",
    "Correction Logic"
  ],
